<p class=MsoNormal><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>               
</span>longDesc: &quot;My first fond memory of ‘us’ is when you invited me to
your birthday party. It was honestly quite unexpected from my end, and I cannot
put into words the excitement, joy and hope I felt when you invited me. When I
got the invite, I’m pretty sure I texted my friends, and they were like ‘you’re
kidding’. One of my friends even asked me if I asked to go to your birthday
party instead of being invited haha. I think that’s how unbelievable it was,
and that’s how big of a crush I had on you during that time. In all honesty,
you and your friends made a genius move to allow me to bring a plus one because
I think I would’ve been too nervous to attend! Your party was definitely a
rollercoaster of emotions for me. That night, I thought that you either still
liked Will, or you guys were dating, especially with him being able to grab
that seat next to you. In that moment, I felt quite sad haha. The rest of the
night went well, and we were able to ride our scooters together! (although we
fell behind sooo much that kyle had to go back to check on us) I was honestly
quite scared of you falling off if I tried driving so I let you ride your own
scooter. And, because we valued our lives so much, we decided to teach you how
to ride a scooter down the sketchiest alleyway ever. I also remember going to
the casino, and then bar hopping around and then playing never have I ever, and
kiss marry kill. My hopes rose again when you said out of the three, you’d go
out on a date with me, but they were killed once again when you said you’d kiss
me, and marry Will. I now understand you were trying not to be obvious, but I
think that night you made me sad twice lol, and I was so confused on whether
you liked me or not. I think I thought to myself like why won’t she marry me or
date me? We then went to karaoke later that night, and when we had to leave, I
got my first ever hug from you, and I think our relationship was all uphill
from then on! I remember walking out the karaoke place, and calling albin and
sooking and crying to him about everything. I also remember going home, getting
locked out the house, and getting yelled at but at that moment i didnt care at
all, and I went to go find soju to drink in the dark haha. Although that night
was a rollercoaster, I think I sometimes look back and laugh at my thought
process, and it is going to go down as one of my most memorable nights ever, if
not my most memorable one. Maybe our children will hear this story.&quot;,<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>                </span>quote:
&quot;JJ did not sook about this the night he got home, or the days after ~ The
ghost in JJ's room&quot;,<o:p></o:p></p>

