<p class=MsoNormal><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>               
</span>longDesc: &quot;This was our first ever ‘date’ or ‘hangout’ but hey, you
can decide on what you wanted it to be. I remember asking my friends how to ask
you to go, and being so nervous when i sent that message. Luckily, the pretty
girl i asked to go to the cinemas with me said yes! I remember you getting lost
in Elizabeth, and coming maybe 15 minutes late. Leading into the movie, I
wasn’t sure on whether I was more scared and nervous to watch the movie, or
whether I was more scared and nervous to be sitting next to the girl that I had
a crush on! During the movie, there were many times where I wanted to hold your
hand, but I wasn’t sure if that was our dynamic yet. I also remember you
laughing at literally every scary scene, and thinking back, the signs were
there. After the movie, I gave you a Labubu, and some mooncakes that were
somewhat expensive for their size. I thought that was it after, and was
initially planning to leave leave after that because I wasn’t sure what to do,
but you initiated something related to driving me and I was more than up for
it! I think driving us around, going to the hungry jacks drive through and
nearly crashing, getting some ice creams, and then talking for a while was
honestly really sweet, and I was another chance to get to know you. I remember
you said in the car that you wanted me to stay longer, and I thought that was
really sweet, and I think those were some of the hints that I desperately
needed to know that you possibly liked me back! I remember when we were leaving,
since some got lost on the way to Elizabeth, I decided to lead the way back to
your house so that you wouldn’t get lost another time. (especially since it was
dark already) I think that was the simpiest thing that I had done at the time,
and I don’t regret it one bit. I also remember getting to your house and asking
for a hug by saying ‘hug!’ and when I left, I was like, omg why’d I say it like
that.&quot;,<o:p></o:p></p>

